! REPRODUCER, an ASSEMBLER finding (docs/NEXT.md, "G2.1 CHAPTER 4: WHAT
! THE ASSEMBLER REFUSES IN A DD(N)").  strap_asm.py refuses this deck:
!
!   cannot parse DD(N) literal '1/720'
!
! The statement is C22-6578 printed p.46 (Problem 4.11), CONST's third
! card: "DD(N), 1/3628800, 1/362880, 1/40320, 1/5040, 1/720".
! C28-6129 printed p.27-28 (PDF 31-32): "Arithmetic expressions, that
! is, combination of two or more numbers by means of addition,
! subtraction, multiplication and division to form one data entry, are
! permitted in all DD statements regardless of the use mode specified";
! its example e is "DD(N), 1/3, 472*351, 4-7*5/21 S 4".
!
! When it assembles, RECIP must hold 1/720 as a normalized word,
! exponent -9, fraction 512/720 = .7111...: 013B 60B6 0B60 B600 if
! STRAP truncates.  The manual does not say whether it truncates or to
! how many bits it carries the division (strap_asm.py _dd_normalized).
! tests/check_problem_4_dd_refusals.py asserts the refusal and will
! fail, on purpose, the day this is built.

START   BEW, $
RECIP   DD(N), 1/720
        END, START
